# ── Frontend (read at request time — no rebuild needed) ───────────────
# URLs the BROWSER uses to reach the APIs. These are resolved per request from
# the container's environment, so `docker compose up -d frontend` is enough to
# apply a change — no rebuild.
#
# NOTE: this file is read by `docker compose`. It does NOT reach a host
# `npm run dev`, which only reads frontend/.env.local.
#
# Behind a reverse proxy (the argus-halo demo's Caddy), point each service at a
# PATH PREFIX on the proxy's own origin:
#     ARGUS_CURATOR_URL=/api/curator
#     ARGUS_LENS_URL=/api/lens
# An EMPTY value means the origin root (`/scan/folder`). That works for at most
# ONE backend: the six services all expose `/health`, and curator+lens both
# expose `/folders` while curator+quarry both expose `/thumb`, so a shared root
# is ambiguous. Prefer prefixes when more than one service is proxied.
ARGUS_LENS_URL=http://localhost:8100
ARGUS_CURATOR_URL=http://localhost:8101
# argus-quarry provenance server (the /gallery page).
ARGUS_QUARRY_URL=http://localhost:8102
# argus-forge training bridge (the ExportPanel "forge training config" step).
ARGUS_FORGE_URL=http://localhost:8103
# argus-proof post-training evaluation (the /proof review view + run trigger).
ARGUS_PROOF_URL=http://localhost:8104
# argus-atlas georeferenced map bakes (the /atlas page).
ARGUS_ATLAS_URL=http://localhost:8105
# argus-darkroom guarded generation (the /darkroom page).
ARGUS_DARKROOM_URL=http://localhost:8106

# Footer links to the standalone demo UIs, as the browser reaches them. A UI left
# unset gets no link.
# ARGUS_LIGHTBOX_URL=https://lightbox.example.com
# ARGUS_CULL_URL=https://cull.example.com
# ARGUS_SAFELIGHT_URL=https://safelight.example.com
# ARGUS_SIGHTLINE_URL=http://localhost:3107
# ARGUS_MASK_URL=http://localhost:8109

# Curator SPA mode.
#   demo — read-only bundled sample scan; no curator backend required (public demo).
#   live — real scans/exports against ARGUS_CURATOR_URL. Use this when you
#          bring up the curator/full profile below. (`local` is a legacy alias.)
ARGUS_CURATOR_UI_MODE=demo

# Paths as seen INSIDE the curator container (the compose mounts DATASET_DIR/OUTPUT_DIR
# there). These are the defaults the folder picker and export panel start from.
# Compose supplies these two values; running the image outside compose without
# them leaves the folder picker blank.
ARGUS_CURATOR_SOURCE_PATH=/data/images
ARGUS_CURATOR_OUTPUT_PATH=/data/out

# 1 is for your own library. /curate and /darkroom offer the adult-* SingGuard
# policies still under evaluation, and nothing restricts deleting: /curate can
# delete ANY scanned image from disk, and /darkroom can delete records and images
# outright, audit trail included. Every delete still takes a click and a confirm.
# Nothing else loosens: move, bakes, fetches and NSFW keep their own flags.
# ARGUS_DEVMODE is the same switch and wins if both are set. CURATOR_DEVMODE=0 or
# DARKROOM_DEVMODE=0 keeps the policies but not that service's deletes.
# DEVMODE=1

# Content-Security-Policy on every page (frontend/src/lib/csp.ts). Scripts run
# only with the per-request nonce Next and the layout stamp on them, plus what
# they load ('strict-dynamic'); no plugins, <base> or framing. It does not limit
# where the backends live. enforce (default) | report-only (violations go to the
# browser console only) | off. Use report-only first if a reverse proxy or
# extension injects scripts into the page. Any other value enforces. off drops
# only the policy: X-Frame-Options DENY, nosniff and Referrer-Policy are sent in
# every mode, so studio cannot be embedded in a frame.
# ARGUS_CSP=enforce

# The pre-#56 NEXT_PUBLIC_* names are still honoured as a fallback if you have
# an older .env, but they no longer need a rebuild to take effect. The one that
# is not a straight prefix swap: NEXT_PUBLIC_API_URL is now ARGUS_LENS_URL.

# Browsing the UI from ANOTHER machine (LAN)? Point the ARGUS_*_URLs above at
# this host's IP, and widen curator/forge/atlas CORS to that browser origin — their
# images only allow http://localhost:3000 by default (quarry/proof allow any
# origin). Lens 0.11+ also refuses writes from an unlisted origin with a 403,
# so set LENS_CORS_ORIGINS too. Comma-separated; keep localhost for same-host browsing.
# 203.0.113.x in these examples is a placeholder; use your own host's address.
# CURATOR_CORS_ORIGINS=http://localhost:3000,http://203.0.113.10:3000
# FORGE_CORS_ORIGINS=http://localhost:3000,http://203.0.113.10:3000
# ATLAS_CORS_ORIGINS=http://localhost:3000,http://203.0.113.10:3000
# LENS_CORS_ORIGINS=http://localhost:3000,http://203.0.113.10:3000

# ── Image tags (published GHCR images) ────────────────────────────────
# compose.yaml runs the backends from ghcr.io/smk762/<svc>:${<SVC>_TAG}. Each
# defaults to the release this studio was checked against (the values below),
# so a deploy is reproducible without setting any. Set one to try another
# release, or `latest` to follow each repo's newest.
#   docker compose --profile full pull      # refresh to the current tag
# (frontend has no published image — it is always built from ./frontend.)
# CURATOR_TAG also picks compose.gpu.yaml's image, with `-gpu` appended.
# argus-sightline publishes no image yet: build it with compose.build.yaml.
# argus-forge's `<version>-train` image (torch + sd-scripts, for live POST /run)
# is opt-in: FORGE_TAG=0.2.0-train, on a trusted GPU host only.
CURATOR_TAG=0.15.0
LENS_TAG=0.11.0
QUARRY_TAG=0.4.0
FORGE_TAG=0.2.0
PROOF_TAG=0.2.2
ATLAS_TAG=0.3.1
DARKROOM_TAG=0.2.0
# SURVEY_TAG=0.1.1
# SIGHTLINE_TAG=0.1.0
# MASK_TAG=0.2.0
# OLLAMA_TAG=0.40.16

# ── Suite services (compose profiles) ─────────────────────────────────
# Host directories shared with the backends. Both curator and lens mount
# DATASET_DIR at /data/images so the curate -> caption handoff works.
# Use absolute paths (compose does NOT expand ~). Leave HF_CACHE_DIR unset to
# default to ${HOME}/.cache/huggingface.
DATASET_DIR=./data
OUTPUT_DIR=./out
# HF_CACHE_DIR=/home/you/.cache/huggingface

# argus-quarry (gallery profile) — upstream acquisition of PD/CC0 images,
# grouped into LoRA-training categories (identity/wardrobe/setting/concept).
# QUARRY_HOME is quarry's side-car pool + provenance DB (mounted at /data/quarry).
# It is also mounted read-only into curator/lens so quarry's published symlinks
# (which point back into the pool) resolve inside those containers. Use absolute
# paths. QUARRY_MAX_GB caps the total raw-pool size (0 = unlimited).
QUARRY_HOME=./quarry
QUARRY_MAX_GB=40
# Public-domain metadata archives for /gallery -> Sources: a directory holding
# pd12m/ and megalith/ as written by argus-quarry's
# scripts/fetch_public_domain_metadata.py (links, captions, sizes; ~45 GB with
# PD12M's CLIP embeddings, no photos). Mounted read-only into the quarry server;
# build its search index once with
#   docker compose run --rm argus-quarry-server archives index
# PUBLIC_DOMAIN_DIR=/media/photos/public_domain
# Let the Sources view land a slice in the pool itself (otherwise it hands back
# slice.json + `argus-quarry archives fetch slice.json`). Off by default.
# QUARRY_ALLOW_FETCH=1
# The fetch is a browser POST, which quarry never grants to its default "*"
# CORS, so also list every origin the studio is opened from (argus-quarry
# >= 0.3.1). This replaces "*" for the quarry server's reads too.
# QUARRY_CORS_ORIGINS=http://localhost:3000,http://203.0.113.10:3000
COMMONS_USER_AGENT=argus-quarry/0.2 (contact@example.com)

# Optional Immich integration (lens /immich/* endpoints: caption straight from
# an Immich album, or pull an album into DATASET_DIR for curation). Create an
# API key in Immich under Account Settings -> API Keys. Leave unset to disable.
# IMMICH_URL=http://immich:2283
# IMMICH_API_KEY=

# argus-proof (proof/full profiles) — post-training evaluation runs.
# The generation engine's model tree (ComfyUI layout: checkpoints/ + loras/),
# mounted read-only at /data/models so run manifests SHA256-pin the weights and
# GET /models can populate the /proof pickers. Absolute paths. If your ComfyUI
# also loads from an extra_model_paths tree, point MODELS_EXTRA_DIR at it.
MODELS_DIR=./models
# MODELS_EXTRA_DIR=/path/to/extra_models/models-hot
# Backend that generates the eval grid, and how the proof CONTAINER reaches it.
# host.docker.internal targets a ComfyUI on the compose host (port 8188).
PROOF_BACKEND=comfyui
COMFYUI_BASE_URL=http://host.docker.internal:8188
# pip extras baked into the proof image. Default is light (phash dedup/diversity
# only); "server,cli,score" adds identity/quality/safety scorers (torch stack).
# Only applies to a source build (-f compose.build.yaml); the published image
# ships with server,cli.
PROOF_EXTRAS=server,cli

# argus-atlas (atlas/full profiles) — bake a fantasy map from real terrain.
# DEM_DIR holds the DEMs (GeoTIFF or .vrt, e.g. Copernicus GLO-30) and vector
# layers the /atlas page can name; mounted at /data/dem. Jobs land under
# OUTPUT_DIR/atlas. Bakes go through COMFYUI_BASE_URL (above) using MODELS_DIR.
DEM_DIR=./dem
# Baking needs a GPU (ComfyUI) and is OFF unless set. ATLAS_ALLOW_OSM=1 lets
# the server fetch OSM layers from Overpass itself.
# ATLAS_ALLOW_BAKE=1
# ATLAS_ALLOW_OSM=1
# Your own Overpass endpoint for that fetch. Empty uses atlas's default, the
# public overpass-api.de.
# ATLAS_OVERPASS_URL=
# Optional host dir of style recipes (<name>.json), mounted read-only at
# /data/recipes for the CLI's `chunk`/`chunks --recipe <name>`, e.g.
#   docker compose --profile atlas run --rm argus-atlas argus-atlas chunk --recipe antique ...
# The /atlas page doesn't read recipes. Defaults to ./recipes.
# ATLAS_RECIPES_DIR=./recipes

# argus-darkroom (darkroom profile) — guarded generation at /darkroom. Not part of
# the full profile. It refuses to start without a SingGuard, and none is bundled.
# SINGGUARD_URL is read too, so one value can serve darkroom's own .env format.
# DARKROOM_SINGGUARD_URL=http://host.docker.internal:9150
# The folder ComfyUI lists models from, when that isn't MODELS_DIR.
# DARKROOM_MODELS_DIR=
# Defaults to the bundled nudenet service. Empty: SFW generation is refused.
# DARKROOM_NUDENET_URL=http://nudenet:8080
# Curator's POST /faces?body=true, for the age check on each output.
# DARKROOM_AGE_URL=http://argus-curator:8101
# Both set: prompt expansion is available.
# DARKROOM_OLLAMA_URL=
# DARKROOM_OLLAMA_MODEL=
# DARKROOM_THINKING=cascade
# The checkpoint a form starts on: a name, or a folder under checkpoints/.
# DARKROOM_DEFAULT_CHECKPOINT=sdxl
# 1 lets an NSFW policy enforce. Anything else: SFW only.
# DARKROOM_ALLOW_NSFW=0
# 1 refuses every write, pre-flight included. Records stay readable.
# DARKROOM_READ_ONLY=0
# Name each origin. A wildcard allows reads and refuses every write.
# DARKROOM_CORS_ORIGINS=http://localhost:3000
# Loopback by default: darkroom is not for public hosting.
# DARKROOM_PUBLISH=127.0.0.1:8106

# argus-lens
# hybrid = WD14 (anime/booru tags) + Florence-2 prose. For everyday photos use
# the RAM++ photo tagger instead: ARGUS_BACKEND=hybrid:ram+florence2
ARGUS_BACKEND=hybrid
ARGUS_API_KEY=
# WD14 tags locally + prose from an OpenAI-compatible server (Ollama, vLLM):
#   ARGUS_BACKEND=hybrid:wd14+openai-compat
# The URL is reached from INSIDE the lens container: use the LAN host's IP, or
# host.docker.internal for an Ollama on this machine.
# ARGUS_OPENAI_COMPAT_BASE_URL=http://203.0.113.50:11434/v1
# ARGUS_OPENAI_COMPAT_MODEL=qwen3-vl:8b
# ARGUS_OPENAI_COMPAT_API_KEY=
# Prompt preset (detailed, straightforward, descriptive, booru, count) or literal
# text. Default detailed; straightforward suits Qwen3-VL / JoyCaption for training.
# ARGUS_OPENAI_COMPAT_PROMPT=straightforward
# WD v3 tagger repo (default SmilingWolf/wd-vit-tagger-v3). WD14_CACHE_DIR is the
# host dir mounted as its cache (default ${HOME}/.cache/wd14_tagger).
# WD14_MODEL_REPO=SmilingWolf/wd-eva02-large-tagger-v3
# WD14_CACHE_DIR=/home/you/.cache/wd14_tagger
# LLM rewrite of assembled captions, kept only when it passes lens's post-check.
# On by default against the bundled ollama service (qwen3:8b, pulled on first
# start). ARGUS_REFINE=off disables it; point BASE_URL elsewhere to use another LLM.
# ARGUS_REFINE=off
# ARGUS_REFINE_MODEL=qwen3:8b
# ARGUS_REFINE_BASE_URL=http://ollama:11434/v1
# ARGUS_REFINE_API_KEY=
# ARGUS_REFINE_VARIANTS=all
# RAM_CACHE_DIR=/home/you/.cache/ram_plus
# Sharing the GPU with ComfyUI: release lens's VRAM after N idle seconds.
# ARGUS_IDLE_UNLOAD_S=120
# Set in the GPU section below.
# pip extras baked into the standalone lens image. Default is a self-contained
# local backend; use "server,openai,replicate" for a light cloud-only image.
# Only applies to a source build (-f compose.build.yaml); the published image
# ships with server,local.
LENS_EXTRAS=server,local

# ── Curator detectors ─────────────────────────────────────────────────
# NudeNet is on by default, through the bundled nudenet service. Point this at
# another server running the same image, or set it empty to switch it off.
# ARGUS_CURATOR_NUDENET_URL=http://nudenet:8080
# Seconds per image, and parallel requests. Curator's defaults when unset.
# ARGUS_CURATOR_NUDENET_TIMEOUT=
# ARGUS_CURATOR_NUDENET_WORKERS=
# EraX second detector. Off when empty; there is no published image.
# ARGUS_CURATOR_ERAX_URL=
# Watermark detector for /curate's crops. Off when empty; no server is bundled.
# ARGUS_CURATOR_WATERMARK_URL=
# SingGuard policy check. Off when empty; no server is bundled.
# ARGUS_CURATOR_SINGGUARD_URL=
# ARGUS_CURATOR_SINGGUARD_THINKING=cascade
# Empty sends the image alone.
# ARGUS_CURATOR_SINGGUARD_CONTEXT=age,folder,caption,scene
# ARGUS_CURATOR_SINGGUARD_POLICY_FILE=
# Face attribute, scene and garment models are read from
# ~/.cache/argus_curator/models/. Build them with the argus-curator *-convert
# commands; a missing file leaves that detector reported as unavailable.
# Source builds only (compose.build.yaml): 1 builds the CUDA curator image.
# CURATOR_GPU=0

# ── GPU sharing ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Lens and curator take one GPU job at a time through a shared lock file.
# Defaults to lease with compose.gpu.yaml and none without it.
# ARGUS_GPU_COORDINATOR=lease
# Host directory holding the lock, mounted into both services.
# ARGUS_GPU_LOCK_DIR=/tmp/argus-gpu
# Longest a model waits for the GPU before the job fails (seconds).
# ARGUS_GPU_LEASE_TIMEOUT_S=300

# ── Ports (host side) ─────────────────────────────────────────────────
FRONTEND_PORT=3000
LENS_PORT=8100
CURATOR_PORT=8101
QUARRY_SERVER_PORT=8102
FORGE_PORT=8103
PROOF_PORT=8104
ATLAS_PORT=8105

# argus-survey + argus-sightline (`--profile survey`; build them with compose.build.yaml
# until they are on GHCR). SURVEY_ALLOW_PROCESS=1 lets the UI run steps.
# SURVEY_IN_DIR=./survey-in
# SURVEY_ALLOW_PROCESS=1
# SURVEY_PORT=8107
# SIGHTLINE_PORT=3107

# argus-mask (`--profile mask`) — the talking-face viewer, linked from studio's footer
# (ARGUS_MASK_URL above). Not part of full. Loopback by default: mask has no
# authentication, so reaching the port is access; front it with a TLS proxy for LAN screens.
# MASK_PUBLISH=127.0.0.1:8109
# The faces, one directory per face (a .glb and a manifest.json), mounted read-only.
# MASK_ASSETS_DIR=./mask-assets
# energy: mouth from loudness, CPU only. a2f: an Audio2Face server you run (NVIDIA GPU).
# MASK_DRIVER=energy
# MASK_A2F_URL=http://host.docker.internal:8110
# MASK_FPS=30
# Extra origins allowed to open mask's sockets (its own host always is), e.g. a TLS proxy's.
# MASK_CORS_ORIGINS=https://mask.example.org
# 1 refuses every audio source; viewers still connect.
# MASK_READ_ONLY=0
# TTS stream for POST /speak. Empty: /speak answers 422 (POST /push needs none).
# MASK_TTS_URL=
# MASK_TTS_VOICE=
